+<body>
+<aside class="sidebar">
+<a href="#" class="brand" aria-label="Typeframe home"><span class="brand-icon">tf</span>typeframe<span style="color:#a39b8d;font-size:15px;margin-left:-7px">.</span></a>
+<div class="brand-sub">A LITTLE TYPE EXPLORATION</div>
+<div class="nav-label">WORKSPACE</div>
+<nav class="nav" aria-label="Workspace"><a href="#overview"><span class="nav-icon">▦</span>Overview</a><a href="#playground" class="active"><span class="nav-icon">T<span style="font-size:12px">t</span></span>Font playground</a><a href="#themes"><span class="nav-icon">◐</span>Themes</a><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-size-adjust" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><span class="nav-icon">▤</span>Resources <span style="margin-left:auto;font-size:11px">↗</span></a></nav>
+<div class="sidebar-bottom"><div class="version"><span class="dot"></span>CSS, a little more considered.</div><p>Made for the details.<br>Typeframe v1.0</p></div>
+</aside>
+<main>
+<header class="topbar"><div class="crumb">Workspace <span style="color:#c4beb2">/</span> <strong>Font playground</strong></div><a class="doc-link" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-size-adjust" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">CSS documentation <span>↗</span></a></header>
+<div class="workspace" id="overview">
+<div class="page-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span></span>The font playground</div><h1>Different fonts. Same rhythm.</h1><p class="intro">Bring your type into balance. Explore how modern CSS keeps mixed fonts<br> feeling consistent, and gives independent themes room to be themselves.</p></div><button class="copy-button" id="copy-css"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="11" rx="1.5"/><path d="M12 7V3H3v10h4"/></svg><span>Copy CSS</span></button></div>
+<div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Playground view"><button class="tab active" id="preview-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="preview-panel"><span>▧</span>Live preview</button><button class="tab" id="css-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="css-panel"><span style="font-size:12px">&lt;/&gt;</span>CSS</button></div>
+<div id="preview-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="preview-tab">
+<section id="playground"><div class="section-top"><h2 class="section-title"><span class="number">01</span>Mixed fonts, in harmony</h2><label class="size-control">Size <input type="range" id="font-size" min="16" max="30" value="22" aria-label="Preview font size"><output id="size-value">22px</output><button type="button" class="reset" id="reset" title="Reset playground">↺</button></label></div><p class="section-description">One text block. Multiple font families. A naturally consistent x-height.</p>
+<div class="card"><div class="card-toolbar"><div class="controls"><label class="field">Text font <select id="text-font"><option value="'DM Sans', sans-serif">DM Sans</option><option value="Arial, sans-serif">Arial</option><option value="Georgia, serif">Georgia</option><option value="Verdana, sans-serif">Verdana</option></select></label><label class="field">Code font <select id="code-font"><option value="'IBM Plex Mono', monospace">IBM Plex Mono</option><option value="'Courier New', monospace">Courier New</option><option value="monospace">System Mono</option></select></label></div><div class="adjust-control">Auto normalize <button id="normalize" class="switch" role="switch" aria-checked="true" aria-label="Auto normalize font heights"></button></div></div>
+<div class="specimen"><div class="specimen-label">THE MIXED FONT SPECIMEN</div><p id="mixed-fonts-container">Good typography is in the details. A little <code>inline code</code> should feel<br class="wide-break"> right at home with the words around it. Even <code>const hello = "world";</code><br class="wide-break"> deserves a little visual harmony.</p></div>
+<div class="card-bottom"><code class="code-line"><span class="property">font-size-adjust</span>: <span class="value" id="auto-code-value">from-font</span>;</code><span class="badge" id="normalize-badge">Automatic x-height matching</span></div></div></section>
+<section id="themes" class="section-two"><h2 class="section-title"><span class="number">02</span>A theme of its own</h2><p class="section-description">An independent space with a fixed metric. Consistent proportions, by design.</p>
+<div class="card"><div class="theme-card"><div class="theme-preview" id="independent-theme-container"><div class="theme-heading"><span>THE EDITORIAL THEME</span><span class="theme-tag">Independent theme</span></div><h2>A different voice. Its own balance.</h2><p>Some spaces call for a different character. This theme pairs thoughtful<br class="wide-break"> prose with <code>small details</code>, with its proportions set to a fixed rhythm.</p></div><div class="theme-settings"><div class="settings-label">X-height ratio</div><div class="metric-value">0.50 <span class="fixed">FIXED</span></div><p>An explicit metric keeps this theme<br>independent of the surrounding type.</p><select id="theme" class="theme-select" aria-label="Theme palette"><option value="sage">Sage · Editorial</option><option value="ink">Ink · Editorial</option><option value="clay">Clay · Editorial</option></select></div></div><div class="card-bottom"><code class="code-line"><span class="property">font-size-adjust</span>: <span class="value">0.5</span>;</code><span class="badge">Explicit metric override</span></div></div></section>
+<div class="info-box"><span class="info-icon">i</span><div><strong>A small property. A big difference.</strong> <code>font-size-adjust</code> preserves perceived text size across font families.<br>Use <code>from-font</code> for automatic balance, or a numeric value for precise control. <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-size-adjust" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" style="color:#9c6a48;white-space:nowrap">Explore the property ↗</a></div></div>
+</div>
+<div id="css-panel" class="hidden" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="css-tab"><pre class="code-panel"><code id="css-source"></code></pre></div>
+<footer class="workspace-footer"><span>Built on native CSS. Designed for the details.</span><span class="footer-right"><span class="dot"></span><span id="support-status">Modern CSS, naturally.</span></span></footer>
+</div>
+</main>
+<div role="status" class="toast hidden" id="toast"></div>
+<script>
+const $ = s => document.querySelector(s);
+const mixed = $('#mixed-fonts-container');
+const state = { normalize: true, size: 22, text: "'DM Sans', sans-serif", code: "'IBM Plex Mono', monospace" };
+function source() { return `/* Automatically balance mixed font families */\n#mixed-fonts-container {\n  font-family: ${state.text};\n  font-size: ${state.size}px;\n  font-size-adjust: ${state.normalize ? 'from-font' : 'none'};\n  line-height: 1.85;\n}\n\n#mixed-fonts-container code {\n  font-family: ${state.code};\n  font-size: 1em;\n}\n\n/* Give an independent theme its own fixed proportions */\n#independent-theme-container {\n  font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;\n  font-size-adjust: 0.5;\n}`; }
+function update() {
+ mixed.style.fontFamily = state.text;
+ mixed.style.fontSize = state.size + 'px';
+ mixed.style.fontSizeAdjust = state.normalize ? 'from-font' : 'none';
+ mixed.querySelectorAll('code').forEach(el => el.style.fontFamily = state.code);
+ $('#size-value').value = state.size + 'px';
+ $('#normalize').setAttribute('aria-checked', state.normalize);
+ $('#auto-code-value').textContent = state.normalize ? 'from-font' : 'none';
+ $('#normalize-badge').textContent = state.normalize ? 'Automatic x-height matching' : 'Original font proportions';
+ $('#css-source').textContent = source();
+}
+$('#text-font').addEventListener('change', e => { state.text = e.target.value; update(); });
+$('#code-font').addEventListener('change', e => { state.code = e.target.value; update(); });
+$('#font-size').addEventListener('input', e => { state.size = Number(e.target.value); update(); });
+$('#normalize').addEventListener('click', () => { state.normalize = !state.normalize; update(); });
+$('#theme').addEventListener('change', e => document.body.dataset.theme = e.target.value);
+$('#reset').addEventListener('click', () => { state.normalize = true; state.size = 22; $('#text-font').selectedIndex = 0; $('#code-font').selectedIndex = 0; state.text = $('#text-font').value; state.code = $('#code-font').value; $('#font-size').value = 22; update(); });
+function showTab(css) { $('#preview-panel').classList.toggle('hidden', css); $('#css-panel').classList.toggle('hidden', !css); ['preview', 'css'].forEach(name => { const active = (name === 'css') === css; $('#' + name + '-tab').classList.toggle('active', active); $('#' + name + '-tab').setAttribute('aria-selected', active); $('#' + name + '-tab').tabIndex = active ? 0 : -1; }); }
+$('#preview-tab').addEventListener('click', () => showTab(false));
+$('#css-tab').addEventListener('click', () => showTab(true));
+$('.tabs').addEventListener('keydown', e => { if (['ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'Home', 'End'].includes(e.key)) { e.preventDefault(); const css = e.key === 'End' || (e.key !== 'Home' && $('#preview-tab').getAttribute('aria-selected') === 'true'); showTab(css); $(css ? '#css-tab' : '#preview-tab').focus(); } });
+let toastTimer;
+function notify(message) { $('#toast').textContent = message; $('#toast').classList.remove('hidden'); clearTimeout(toastTimer); toastTimer = setTimeout(() => $('#toast').classList.add('hidden'), 2800); }
+$('#copy-css').addEventListener('click', async () => { try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(source()); notify('CSS copied to clipboard'); } catch { showTab(true); notify('Select the CSS to copy it'); } });
+$('.nav').querySelectorAll('a[href^="#"]').forEach(link => link.addEventListener('click', () => { showTab(false); $('.nav').querySelectorAll('a').forEach(a => a.classList.toggle('active', a === link)); }));
+if (!CSS.supports('font-size-adjust', 'from-font')) $('#support-status').textContent = 'Use a modern browser for font adjustment';
+update();
+</script>
+</body>
+</html>
